WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:08.300
there's a lot of surprises, other than the reference to the PCSK9 outcomes trials. So I think

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:15.080
we're trying to understand that, you know, given that usually we don't get to refer to somebody

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:21.460
else's outcome studies. And I think with respect to the, other than that, nothing that changes our

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.900
view. I mean, look, our belief is that there's a significant segment of the market, and this is a

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.940
huge market, and the number of patients who are not at goal.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:36.040
For lipid lowering to reach their lipid targets is significant in the United States. You know,

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:41.280
we're talking about here a 70 million patient segment overall, you know, a significant portion

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.300
of these patients who are not at goal. And so I think the opportunity for the PCSK9s is,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.840
for these advanced lipid lowering therapies is significant. And we see that there's ongoing

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.040
demand for patients who want infrequently administered therapies and physicians who

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.820
want to provide the therapy as well.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.900
In the physician-administered setting. So I think the fact that we're not participating

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:09.900
in the gross-to-net battle that will ensue between the monoclonal antibodies and the orals

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.960
actually are in a segment that's insulated from that, I think is a strong position in the longer

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:25.640
run for our goals of a $4 billion to $5 billion plus product. Now, with respect to the food effect,

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.960
I think it remains to be seen. I mean, I think clearly the eight-hour fast plus the

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:35.820
30, I think it's a 30-minute or so post-fast in this particular drug. But, you know, I think

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.320
we'll have to see because obviously patients can find ways to manage that. And I would say there

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.500
are other competitors coming that, as far as we understand, may not have the food effect. So

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:52.120
given that, I think we just have to focus on our segment and focus on the patients that we can

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:59.360
reach in that Part B buy-and-bill setting in the U.S. I do want to pitch again outside of the U.S.,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:01:59.940
particularly in the U.S.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.600
In Asia, we see very strong uptake for SIRNAs. And we think that in some, it's a very country-by-country

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.780
situation as to, you know, what kind of profile people are looking for in the medicines. And at

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.800
least in Asia and Middle East, we see a high demand for SIRNAs. It gives us a lot of confidence.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:17.800
Thank you.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:26.400
Thank you. Your next question comes from the line of Sachin Jain from Bank of America. Please go

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:26.720
ahead.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.600
Hi, thanks for the follow-up. I just had a one.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.420
Hi, Sachin.

